because blockchain time is a primary research clock.

==================================================
NUMERIC PRECISION
==================================================

Do not represent large blockchain integer values using floating-point numbers where precision could be lost.

Prefer:

string-encoded integer base units

plus

optional normalized decimal representation.

Example:

{
  "raw_amount": "1000000000000000000",
  "decimals": 18,
  "display_amount": "1.0"
}

==================================================
ADDRESS FORMAT
==================================================

Store canonical hexadecimal address.

Validate length.

Validate format.

Use checksum representation where supported.

Do not:

truncate

guess missing characters

or normalize two different addresses into one identity.

==================================================
HASH FORMAT
==================================================

For transaction hashes and cryptographic digests preserve:

algorithm where applicable

full value

Do not publish abbreviated hashes as canonical database identifiers.

